Z||000002||Songman||06-19-2001||04:35 PM||||No, they do not... although I don't know what case markings to look for to tell which is which.<P>If the tranny is still in the car, you can check the RPOs. I am not sure of the years but here are RPOs for 4-speed trannies...<P>MY7 4-speed manual transmission (lsuzu)<BR>MY8 4-speed manual transmission (Muncie) 3.32 ratio<BR>M17 4-speed manual transmission (Muncie) 3.65 ratio<BR>M19 4-speed manual transmission (Muncie) 4.10 ratio<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||KRMFiero||06-19-2001||05:34 PM||||Gears confuse the hell out of me...   4.20 gear that is a bigger gear, from what i understand thats for more top end/more speed<P>a gear say 2.83 (I remember seeing a tranny for soem car with that gear final)   would be slower but have better acceleration/do bettr burn outs<P>am i right or no?||||reg||1
Z||000004||85Josh||06-19-2001||05:50 PM||||KRM, you've got it backwards. Numerically higher gears reduce the engine speed more, resulting in faster acceleration by allowing the engine to get into its powerband sooner, but the engine reaches redline at a lower actual speed. Numerically lower gears,I.E. 2.83's, spin the tires closer to the actual engine speed, so low speeds, like at takeoff, are lower in the powerband, or below it. They do increase top speed, since the wheels rotate closer to engine speed. Hope this isn't more confusing!<P>Moneypit, are you saying this is for a QuadFour conversion? I thought the Q4 used a different bellhousing bolt pattern. Are you planning to make an adapter to mate the engine to tranny? <BR>OK, read the post again! Is the Muncie 4-speed ring and pinon set a bolt-in for a Q4 Getrag? Sound like the car will be really awesome, also went to the site to check it out!<P>------------------<BR>85 2M4(Lil' Bit)<P>[This message has been edited by 85Josh (edited 06-19-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by 85Josh (edited 06-19-2001).]||||reg||1
